  "articleBody": "When upgrading garage trim, baseboards require special installation techniques because of their proximity to the concrete slab. Standard interior trim installed flush against a garage slab often wicks moisture directly out of the concrete, which leads to swelling, mold, and premature decay. Proper installation requires leaving a deliberate expansion and drainage gap above the slab rather than pinning boards flat to the floor.\n\nChoosing the right material makes all the difference. While MDF works well in climate-controlled indoor living areas, it deteriorates quickly if exposed to damp garage conditions, car runoff, or wash water. Solid pine or moisture-resistant trim profiles handle garage environments much better, especially when all cut ends and back faces are sealed with primer before fastening.\n\nWhen Professional Guidance Helps:\nGetting clean lines across an uneven garage floor is tough. Concrete slabs slope toward overhead doors for drainage, which means your trim cannot follow a simple horizontal level without creating strange tapering gaps. If your garage walls have damaged drywall, uneven studs, or out-of-square corners, bringing in a seasoned finish contractor ensures every joint stays tight and protected. Abraham Becerra and the crew at HH Remodeling LLC handle complete garage remodels and interior trim across the Denver metro area. Call 303-505-0866 to discuss your trim installation project.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-23"
